Every battery in a large box is flat with probability $0.1$, independently of the others. Two batteries are taken from the box, where $F$ means flat and $W$ means working.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.95]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (N1) at (2.2,1.4);
\coordinate (N2) at (2.2,-1.4);
\coordinate (E1) at (4.8,2.4);
\coordinate (E2) at (4.8,0.7);
\coordinate (E3) at (4.8,-0.7);
\coordinate (E4) at (4.8,-2.4);
\draw (O) -- (N1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.1$};
\draw (O) -- (N2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.9$};
\draw (N1) -- (E1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.1$};
\draw (N1) -- (E2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.9$};
\draw (N2) -- (E3) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.1$};
\draw (N2) -- (E4) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.9$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N1) {$F$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N2) {$W$};
\node[right] at (E1) {$F$};
\node[right] at (E2) {$W$};
\node[right] at (E3) {$F$};
\node[right] at (E4) {$W$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the probability that at least one of the two batteries is flat, as a decimal.

