$P(\text{no globe works}) = 0.3 \times 0.3$
$= 0.09$
$P(\text{at least one works}) = 1 - 0.09$
$= 0.91$

foundation.question_text:
A box contains $6$ working and $2$ flat batteries. Two batteries are taken out one after the other without replacement, where $W$ means working and $F$ means flat.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.95]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (N1) at (2.2,1.4);
\coordinate (N2) at (2.2,-1.4);
\coordinate (E1) at (4.8,2.4);
\coordinate (E2) at (4.8,0.7);
\coordinate (E3) at (4.8,-0.7);
\coordinate (E4) at (4.8,-2.4);
\draw (O) -- (N1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{6}{8}$};
\draw (O) -- (N2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{2}{8}$};
\draw (N1) -- (E1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{5}{7}$};
\draw (N1) -- (E2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{2}{7}$};
\draw (N2) -- (E3) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{6}{7}$};
\draw (N2) -- (E4) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{1}{7}$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N1) {$W$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N2) {$F$};
\node[right] at (E1) {$W$};
\node[right] at (E2) {$F$};
\node[right] at (E3) {$W$};
\node[right] at (E4) {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the probability that at least one of the two batteries is flat, as a fraction in simplest form.

foundation.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.95]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (N1) at (2.2,1.4);
\coordinate (N2) at (2.2,-1.4);
\coordinate (E1) at (4.8,2.4);
\coordinate (E2) at (4.8,0.7);
\coordinate (E3) at (4.8,-0.7);
\coordinate (E4) at (4.8,-2.4);
\draw (O) -- (N1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{6}{8}$};
\draw (O) -- (N2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{2}{8}$};
\draw (N1) -- (E1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{5}{7}$};
\draw (N1) -- (E2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{2}{7}$};
\draw (N2) -- (E3) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{6}{7}$};
\draw (N2) -- (E4) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{1}{7}$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N1) {$W$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N2) {$F$};
\node[right] at (E1) {$W\quad \frac{30}{56}$};
\node[right] at (E2) {$F\quad \frac{12}{56}$};
\node[right] at (E3) {$W\quad \frac{12}{56}$};
\node[right] at (E4) {$F\quad \frac{2}{56}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$P(\text{no flat battery}) = \frac{6}{8} \times \frac{5}{7}$
$= \frac{30}{56}$
$P(\text{at least one flat}) = 1 - \frac{30}{56}$
$= \frac{26}{56}$
$= \frac{13}{28}$

